{
  "_readme": [
    "Ground truth for eval/vision-bench.mjs: what a careful human reader sees on each plate,",
    "and the energy/macros they would expect a food tracker to report for it.",
    "",
    "Every nutrient is a [low, high] BAND, not a point. Portion estimation from a single",
    "uncalibrated photo is genuinely uncertain — a benchmark demanding one exact number would",
    "reward overfitting to these 20 photos instead of measuring whether the app is useful.",
    "The bands are what a dietitian would accept as 'that's the right answer for this photo':",
    "roughly ±30% around the considered estimate, wider where the serving itself is ambiguous",
    "(a whole pizza on a board, a pan of rice — you cannot know how much of it is one portion).",
    "",
    "dishes[].id must exist in app/public/data/nutrition-db.json. `optional: true` marks a dish",
    "that is genuinely in the photo but which a reasonable person might not log (tea, a garnish,",
    "a condiment smear) — it never counts against recall, and naming it is never spurious.",
    "",
    "Estimates use FNDDS per-100g values, so a miss here means the pipeline is wrong, not that",
    "the arithmetic disagrees with a different food database."
  ],
  "_aliasNote": "Applied to BOTH the expected and the predicted id before comparing. Only for distinctions a person would not make on a photo — every chutney is 'a chutney' — never for foods whose calories differ materially (plain dosa vs masala dosa are separate dishes and must be told apart). The `lib:` entries are the shipped dish library's own name for a food the USDA core already carries; each was checked against that rule and none differs by more than 4% per 100 g. Four of them exist because the note on the photo says one thing and its dish id says another — the note is the one that was written while looking at the picture.",
  "acceptableAliases": {
    "chutney": "any-chutney",
    "coconut-chutney": "any-chutney",
    "green-chutney": "any-chutney",
    "medu-vada": "vada",
    "momo": "dumplings",
    "gyoza": "dumplings",
    "tomato-chutney": "any-chutney",
    "onion-chutney": "any-chutney",
    "peanut-chutney": "any-chutney",
    "lib:idli-plain": "idli",
    "lib:white-rice-cooked": "plain-rice",
    "lib:dal-makhani": "dal",
    "lib:chicken-burger-fried": "hamburger",
    "lib:garlic-naan": "naan",
    "lib:raita": "yogurt-plain"
  },
